# O1 smoke test: OPES_EXPANDED, multithermal-multibaric, on UiO-66 (456 atoms) in LAMMPS.
# Written by hand: hyogo plumed_make_input has no OPES bias or ENERGY/VOLUME CVs (G40).
# Units: A, eV, ps, so PRESSURE is in eV/A^3 (1 bar = 6.2415e-07, 1 GPa = 6.2415e-03).
UNITS LENGTH=A ENERGY=eV TIME=ps
ene: ENERGY
vol: VOLUME
# The thermostat is at 300 K and the barostat at 1 bar (TEMP / PRESSURE must match fix npt).
ecv: ECV_MULTITHERMAL_MULTIBARIC ARG=ene,vol TEMP=300 PRESSURE=6.2415e-07 TEMP_MIN=300 TEMP_MAX=600 PRESSURE_MIN=6.2415e-07 PRESSURE_MAX=6.2415e-03
# Smoke-test settings: PACE 50, bias switched on after 10 x 50 = 500 steps of observation.
opes: OPES_EXPANDED ARG=ecv.* PACE=50 OBSERVATION_STEPS=10 FILE=DELTAFS PRINT_STRIDE=500
PRINT ARG=ene,vol,opes.bias STRIDE=50 FILE=COLVAR
